OL,3,Q]Wjjj S#!!""#"""#"!
OL,4,  Wjjj GENGLAND IN THE WEST INDIES
OL,5,F
OL,6,FEngland have fought their way back into
OL,7,Fthe crucial third Test - largely thanks
OL,8,Fto fast bowler Greg Thombs and batsmen
OL,9,FGraham Gooch and David Gower.
OL,10,F
OL,11,FThey were 110 for one at close on the
OL,12,Fsecond day, in reply to the West Indies
OL,13,Ffirst innings of 418.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FThombs had a new ball burst of four for
OL,16,F14 as the West Indies lost their last
OL,17,Fseven wickets for just 57 runs.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FEngland were in early trouble with the
OL,20,Floss of Tim Robinson, out for three,
OL,21,Fbut Gooch (46no) and Gower (51no)
OL,22,Fresponded bravely to the challenge.
OL,23,Q                     A]CFrom 22-03-86
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
